cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Relational Justice Analysis (RJA)"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Behnam Shad"
    given-names: "Klaus"
    affiliation: "University of Luxembourg, Luxembourg Centre for Contemporary and Digital History (C²DH)"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3601-9024"
repository-code: "https://github.com/klausbehnamshad/relational-justice-analysis"
abstract: >-
  RJA is a theory-driven, rule-based and auditable infrastructure for reconstructing how justice
  claims are socially organized in qualitative interview data. v2.0 replaces the earlier scalar
  intensity model with a disaggregated relational model (justice dimensions, relational configuration,
  vulnerability, residue, audit trail) and ships with an inter-coder reliability study (two blind LLM
  coders and two independent human coders) establishing a three-tier reliability profile.
keywords:
  - relational justice
  - qualitative interview analysis
  - inter-coder reliability
  - computational social science
  - recognition theory
  - digital humanities
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-06-06"
